{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules","id":1456148,"title":"[V5] Using Disciplines in Combat - a mess of unclear rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-04T12:53:41-07:00","id":1456148,"title":"[V5] Using Disciplines in Combat - a mess of unclear rules","content":"Ok, so I was really digging V5 corebook to try to understand probably one of the worst explained combat rules in history of RPG corebooks (I like V5 otherwise mind you). My biggest grip was using Disciplines in combat. When you can use them, do they take action/turn etc. <b>Do you know how it was supposed to work RAW?</b><br /> <br /> So after studying book for quite some time those are bits that I put together in hope to finally have some clear answers:<br /> <br /> 1. Actions take Turn. You can only do one action per turn<br /> 2. Rouse Checks are generally not considered actions. Mending or Blood Surge is not considered an action since they are reflexive for vampires.<br /> 3. Disciplines are Rouse Checks (those that are not passive which are, obviously, always on) too to activate them.<br /> 4. However, &quot;Discipline Usage&quot; at page 244 says &quot;Unless otherwise stated, a vampire can activate a Discipline <b>at any time</b>; this takes little time <b>or</b> overt action&quot;.<br /> <br /> I want you to focus on: it takes little time OR action. So it's one or either... It's still not helping, I know but bear with me.<br /> <br /> 5. So what Disciplines take and do not take an action? That's a mess here.<br /> <br /> We will take a look at couple powers here to compare description and their effect and use logic (something that authors forgot when writing combat rules) to determite how they interact with combat:<br /> <br /> A) Compel from Dominate<br /> B) Dread Gaze from Presence.<br /> C) Toughness<br /> D) Lightning Strike<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> Compel from Dominate can be used in combat. However you need to not only lock eyes with enemy but also speak a command. This is not something that is instant. Description of Compel in corebook says &quot;With eye contact, the vampire can issue the victim a single-action command, no longer than a short sentence, to be obeyed to the letter. It must be possible to complete the command in a single turn&quot;. So the question is: vampire sees enemy pulling gun at them, aiming at him, he locks eyes and say &quot;Run away!&quot;. I would say that here considering time to lock eyes and say can be considered using action. So Vampire won't have time for anything else. Who goes first? Unclear, so I guess ST will have to decide.<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze only needs to &quot;Displaying their fangs, their face twisted in a predatory grimace&quot;. I think we can all agree this is way faster than Compel to use. Also decscription of Dread Gaze says &quot;Mortals are unable to act other than in their own defense, backing off for a turn&quot;. So enemy loses turn. Not next turn, but turn. This implies that Dread Gaze should be able to work before &quot;physical action&quot; becase otherwise if enemy can make attack before Dread Gaze the whole point of it &quot;Mortals are unable to act&quot; would be pointless.<br /> <br /> And then we have Fortitude powers:<br /> <br /> Toughness has nothing about when you can activate it. Let me remember you that all Rouse Checks in general like Blood Surge or Mending are reflexive. Toughness seems to take absolutely not effort or time to activate or anything. It just works. Description say nothing about it not being able to be activated when you see enemy taking a shot at you from rifle. So question is: can you activate Toughness and then go and attack enemy in same turn? Unclear becasue there are no clear rules about Disciplines!<br /> <br /> And then we have Lightning Strike:<br /> <br /> It definitely is Disciplie activation. Yet again description says NOTHING about it being reflexive, action etc. It's part of attack action. So you can make Attack Action (melee/brawl) and AT THE SAME time do Rouse Check to activate Discipline. It's not something that only Celerity can do becasue again - there is nothing in rules saying that Celerity activates in different manner than other Disciplines. So I guess Brujah can attack and at the same time activate Fist of Kain right? Becasue Lightning Strike only makes enemy unable to defend but it's still Discipline activation as anything else. It doesn't activate faster, it just makes attack go faster but you still need to make attack action + discipline activation. So to follow up you should be able to use Dread Gaze + Shoot enemy since you only need to grim from behind the gun on enemy. Or not? Well, that's the question, right?<br /> <br /> So in the end I have no idea how it should works. Obviously Disciplines should be advantage over mortals so I don't believe they should take actions from Vampires because it doesn't make sense. Other Rouse Checks do not take actions. Dread Gaze obviously is meant to make enemies unable to act in turn. Lighting Strike can be activated as part of melee action attack. Toughness say nothing apart from that it's reducing damage when activated (big help).<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no idea how authors meant that to work.<br /> <br /> Compare to clear V20 rules this is a mess for me as ST becasue I don't want to be unfair to players, but at the same time I would JUST WANT TO KNOW WHAT WAS THE INTENT!<br /> <br /> <b>If you have any idea how RAW should work here I would be grateful for help and explanation.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24341,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","user":"Viben","date":". 08-04-2021, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T17:00:57-07:00","id":1456153,"title":"","content":"The activation of a power is reflective, and unless the power requires a roll it usually shouldn't be an action. Heck, page 219 and 244 makes that clear with these quotes:<ul><li><i><b>In a single turn, a vampire could activate one power of a discipline, take on the Blush of Life, increase an Attribute pool with a Blood Surge, and mend Superficial damage.</b></i></li> <li><i><b>Unless otherwise stated, a vampire can activate a Discipline at any time; this takes little time or overt action. Powers do not usually activate retroactively; they respond to, rather than interrupt, actions taken against the user. A vampire can activate one Discipline power per turn. Any number of powers can be active simultaneously.</b></i></li> </ul>So from this we can easily see most powers are also reflexive, so one could <i><b>Blink</b></i> up to an enemy then attack easily. Now make note that I said most for a reason. Some powers, like say most Dominate powers likely count as using an action 100%. An easy way to see if a power might be an action is if it requires a roll, outside of certain exceptions. For example, Dominate powers like <b><i>Compel</i></b> usually require a roll unless they target an unprepared mortal, making me think it is an action to take. However, <b><i>Blink </i></b>only asks for a roll if the terrain is hazardous, which implies it is a reflexive thing most of the time, and doesn't need to be an action.<br /> <br /> V5 is very abstract so it's usually up to the ST for interpretation. Rules are much more fast and loose with this system, which is a double-edged sword. Ultimately it's up to you, but here's my advice for it:<ul><li>If a power requires you to make a roll most of the time, then it is likely an action. Even if the powers make exceptions for the rolls, they usually call for a roll making it an action. If the power doesn't require a roll except in specific situations then it is likely just reflexive.</li> </ul>I hope this helped, and if not I am sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T17:36:06-07:00","id":1456155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456153#post1456153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The activation of a power is reflective, and unless the power requires a roll it usually shouldn't be an action. Heck, page 219 and 244 makes that clear with these quotes:<ul><li><i><b>In a single turn, a vampire could activate one power of a discipline, take on the Blush of Life, increase an Attribute pool with a Blood Surge, and mend Superficial damage.</b></i></li> <li><i><b>Unless otherwise stated, a vampire can activate a Discipline at any time; this takes little time or overt action. Powers do not usually activate retroactively; they respond to, rather than interrupt, actions taken against the user. A vampire can activate one Discipline power per turn. Any number of powers can be active simultaneously.</b></i></li> </ul><br /> So from this we can easily see most powers are also reflexive, so one could <i><b>Blink</b></i> up to an enemy then attack easily. Now make note that I said most for a reason. Some powers, like say most Dominate powers likely count as using an action 100%. An easy way to see if a power might be an action is if it requires a roll, outside of certain exceptions. For example, Dominate powers like <b><i>Compel</i></b> usually require a roll unless they target an unprepared mortal, making me think it is an action to take. However, <b><i>Blink </i></b>only asks for a roll if the terrain is hazardous, which implies it is a reflexive thing most of the time, and doesn't need to be an action.<br /> <br /> V5 is very abstract so it's usually up to the ST for interpretation. Rules are much more fast and loose with this system, which is a double-edged sword. Ultimately it's up to you, but here's my advice for it:<ul><li>If a power requires you to make a roll most of the time, then it is likely an action. Even if the powers make exceptions for the rolls, they usually call for a roll making it an action. If the power doesn't require a roll except in specific situations then it is likely just reflexive.</li> </ul><br /> I hope this helped, and if not I am sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in simillar way, but for example it doesn't make sense for Dread Gaze which if succesfull make enemy unable to act this turn. If it can't be used before enemy can make his attack then it's useless and I can at least be sure it wasn't meant to be useless. And it does require roll, but the only thing vampire has to do is... make scary face expression which hardly would take an action.<br /> <br /> But overall I agree with your interpretation of rules, I just wished it was clearer how authors intended every single Discipline power to work. Every power has &quot;Duration&quot;. It wouldn't really hurt them to add &quot;Use Cost: Reflexive/Action/Turn&quot; or something like that below it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24341,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","user":"Viben","date":". 08-04-2021, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T18:32:19-07:00","id":1456159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456155#post1456155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in simillar way, but for example it doesn't make sense for Dread Gaze which if succesfull make enemy unable to act this turn. <b>If it can't be used before enemy can make his attack then it's useless and I can at least be sure it wasn't meant to be useless.</b> And it does require roll, but the only thing vampire has to do is... make scary face expression which hardly would take an action.<br /> <br /> But overall I agree with your interpretation of rules, I just wished it was clearer how authors intended every single Discipline power to work. Every power has &quot;Duration&quot;. It wouldn't really hurt them to add &quot;Use Cost: Reflexive/Action/Turn&quot; or something like that below it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Dread Gaze would still be powerful regardless, depending on when used if we go by they can't do anything for the current turn. However, the way it is worded implies that they're inactive for about a turn, which means if they've already acted would mean the next turn is the one they couldn't do anything. IMO the power gets some use one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T00:05:48-07:00","id":1456167,"title":"","content":"The V5 Combat Primer might also help with grokking combat in general: <a href=\"https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Combat_Primer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.v5homebrew.com/wiki/Combat_Primer</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T01:01:57-07:00","id":1456169,"title":"","content":"V5 is that group work where each member of the team writes a chapter but nobody comunicates wich each other so the final document is unclear and full of contradictions<br /> <br /> The book even raises some questions and then refuses to answer them example of this is celerity writting &quot;how fast is fast?&quot; that the game refuses to answer and this was released on the preview so the developers knew this problem.<br /> <br /> This wasnt a difficult to solve problem, just say Speed=Celerity x (Dex + Athletism) and that each point of speed is equal to 5 Km/h.<br /> <br /> The most problematic thing about the game was the hunger system wich divided the fanbase and it was also easy to solve... and they also knew it was divisive<br /> <br /> Personally i think they wanted to incide so much in the &quot;being a vampire sucks&quot; part of the curse and overdid things becuase masquerade was a urban fantasy setting of political horror not an agnst game where the ST emotionally tortures his players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T03:29:59-07:00","id":1456178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book even raises some questions and then refuses to answer them example of this is celerity writting &amp;quot;how fast is fast?&amp;quot; that the game refuses to answer and this was released on the preview so the developers knew this problem.<br /> <br /> This wasnt a difficult to solve problem, just say Speed=Celerity x (Dex + Athletism) and that each point of speed is equal to 5 Km/h.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Your obvious disdain for v5 asside, they did solve that specific problem. The Box &quot;how fast is fast&quot; gives you an estimate about how fast one could go if one would like a &quot;speed equals&quot; rule:<br /> &quot;Usain Bolt, the fastest human being ever timed, runs nearly 45 km/hour. If you assume a dot in Dexterity equals 9 km/hour running flat-out, you have a thumbnail answer to the eternal question \u201cCan my vampire catch that speeding car?\u201d &quot;<br /> Now you can add celerity as more Dex. dots and you have a formular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T05:19:29-07:00","id":1456179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456159#post1456159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually Dread Gaze would still be powerful regardless, depending on when used if we go by they can't do anything for the current turn. However, the way it is worded implies that they're inactive for about a turn, which means if they've already acted would mean the next turn is the one they couldn't do anything. IMO the power gets some use one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the issue: &quot;would mean the next turn&quot;. But in every respectable RPG mechanics you have a difference between turn and next turn. It's quite a bit of a difference how a power/ability works for a player, don't you think? The whole combat system isn't clear enough. And worst part is: it's not a small thing, Disciplines are HUGE part of mechanic of Vampire, it's literally 70% of combat and utility &quot;magic/spells&quot; in game. Yet this was absolutely ignored in mechanics...<br /> <br /> For example there is absolutely NO rules for when two vampires try to Dread Gaze each other. Is it then 2x Roll vs Defense roll (but then who goes first?) or, following combat mechanic, a contested roll of Charisma + Presence and who gets more successes Dread Gazed other one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T07:00:22-07:00","id":1456182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456178#post1456178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your obvious disdain for v5 asside, they did solve that specific problem. The Box &quot;how fast is fast&quot; gives you an estimate about how fast one could go if one would like a &quot;speed equals&quot; rule:<br /> &quot;Usain Bolt, the fastest human being ever timed, runs nearly 45 km/hour. If you assume a dot in Dexterity equals 9 km/hour running flat-out, you have a thumbnail answer to the eternal question \u201cCan my vampire catch that speeding car?\u201d &quot;<br /> Now you can add celerity as more Dex. dots and you have a formular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell how fast is a V5 vampire using celerity 3 blink?<br /> <br /> Nobody can becuase it is a mere narrative effect that says &quot;The vampire swiftly closes in on a foe, engaging or escaping in the blink of an eye.&quot; without a mechanic or math behind<br /> <br /> V5 is a rulebook without rules","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T08:52:24-07:00","id":1456186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456179#post1456179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the issue: &amp;quot;would mean the next turn&amp;quot;. But in every respectable RPG mechanics you have a difference between turn and next turn. It's quite a bit of a difference how a power/ability works for a player, don't you think? The whole combat system isn't clear enough. And worst part is: it's not a small thing, Disciplines are HUGE part of mechanic of Vampire, it's literally 70% of combat and utility &amp;quot;magic/spells&amp;quot; in game. Yet this was absolutely ignored in mechanics...<br /> <br /> For example there is absolutely NO rules for when two vampires try to Dread Gaze each other. Is it then 2x Roll vs Defense roll (but then who goes first?) or, following combat mechanic, a contested roll of Charisma + Presence and who gets more successes Dread Gazed other one?</div> </div> </div> </div>This will sadly go back to V5 being about interpretation at times. It's meant to be a narrative rule set, and so did the earlier editions. Heck combat is also meant to be rare in all VtM games, but yeah having clear rules is also important.<br /> <br /> Ultimately go with what you think best solves the solution at your table, both the attack rolls vs each other or something else. Heck, if this issue is bad enough you can switch to another edition like v20, or even another system like VTR. The Storyteller needs to be able to improvise when needed though, as annoying as that is, and it is very difficult for many people. Just do what is needed for a table and it can turn out great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T12:12:44-07:00","id":1456195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456186#post1456186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This will sadly go back to V5 being about interpretation at times. It's meant to be a narrative rule set, and so did the earlier editions. Heck combat is also meant to be rare in all VtM games, but yeah having clear rules is also important.<br /> <br /> Ultimately go with what you think best solves the solution at your table, both the attack rolls vs each other or something else. Heck, if this issue is bad enough you can switch to another edition like v20, or even another system like VTR. The Storyteller needs to be able to improvise when needed though, as annoying as that is, and it is very difficult for many people. Just do what is needed for a table and it can turn out great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for advice, but I really like V5 for it's tone and that vampires are no longer superheores and they are predators but also hunted. And Hunger system is really nice instead of &quot;mana&quot;. My only grip is unclear mechanics becasue no matter how much system says &quot;it's narrative bla bla&quot; it's still a game. A games need to have clear mechanics.<br /> <br /> I will probably go with the logical conclusion that unless obvious all Disciplines are reflexive and does not take vampire action this turn. This gives huge advantage of vampires vs mortals which should be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T16:03:04-07:00","id":1456206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456182#post1456182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you tell how fast is a V5 vampire using celerity 3 blink?<br /> <br /> Nobody can becuase it is a mere narrative effect that says &quot;The vampire swiftly closes in on a foe, engaging or escaping in the blink of an eye.&quot; without a mechanic or math behind<br /> <br /> V5 is a rulebook without rules</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No edition warring.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T23:33:07-07:00","id":1456215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456148-v5-using-disciplines-in-combat-a-mess-of-unclear-rules?p=1456179#post1456179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the issue: &quot;would mean the next turn&quot;. But in every respectable RPG mechanics you have a difference between turn and next turn. It's quite a bit of a difference how a power/ability works for a player, don't you think? The whole combat system isn't clear enough. And worst part is: it's not a small thing, Disciplines are HUGE part of mechanic of Vampire, it's literally 70% of combat and utility &quot;magic/spells&quot; in game. Yet this was absolutely ignored in mechanics...<br /> <br /> For example there is absolutely NO rules for when two vampires try to Dread Gaze each other. Is it then 2x Roll vs Defense roll (but then who goes first?) or, following combat mechanic, a contested roll of Charisma + Presence and who gets more successes Dread Gazed other one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get why V5 did away with traditional Initiative, but this is why it needs it. I know there's an optional rule for it, but everything functions much better if you use V20 Initiative and turn order rules, without simultaneous roll-offs.<br /> <br /> Though, I think the V20DA Streamlined Combat rules are the best iteration of classic VTM combat. The thing that slows combat down in earlier editions of VTM is the Initiative re-roll for every new round (which most people ignored), the reverse-order declarations phase (ditto), rolling for damage and then rolling for soak. Remove all four of those and it's fast (and lethal).<br /> <br /> V5 removes the damage and soak rolls, but still requires the declaration phase. The GM also has to do the equivalent of calculating Initiative again at the top of every round, because she needs to adjudicate who's going in which order based on their declarations, instead of relying on the Initiative order calculated at the beginning.<br /> <br /> The simple fix, then, is to use traditional Initiative and ignore the declarations phase. Just roll Initiative once and you're set. Make characters take their actions on their turns and a lot of the ambiguity disappears.<br /> <br /> If you want to give passive defences versus attacks (V5 allows multiple rolled defences with minor penalties after all), you could just take half for each defender. So instead of two combatants both rolling their attacks at once, you have them do it one at a time in Initiative order, with the Difficulty of each attack set by half the opponent's defence dice pool.<br /> <br /> Then, if two vampires are both trying to Dread Gaze each other, faster vampire gets in first and slower vampire just has to deal with it when it gets to their turn. It doesn't require any debate to figure it out because the numbers are right there.<br /> <br /> I know some people hate stand and deliver combat, and old school often isn't cool any more, but the problem mostly comes from how combat is narrated (static spaces for combat, no obstacles, no manoeuvring and narration that comprises of 'Uh, you do two damage'). Give people tips on how to make combat dynamic instead and the old school way is fine. And sometimes rules just need to be fine.<br /> <br /> (I also think VTR combat, which is super fast, could be easily ported in if you prefer that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-06-2021, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T01:25:52-07:00","id":1456218,"title":"","content":"For the &quot;what discipline takes an action&quot;-part I play my games as follows: If the discipline does not need something beyond activating it, its &quot;free&quot;. Powers like compel and lightning strike need an &quot;extra action&quot; to take effect (the command / the strike itself) so they need an action to activate. Thoughness and dread gaze do not need something like this, so they are free. If you go with the advanced conflict rules you could also use maneuvers for some of those disciplines (Compel, Scorpion\u00b4s Touch etc.).<br /> <br /> For the &quot;dread gaze vs dread gaze&quot;-part: For me it depends on the situation. That being said, under normal circumstances I would roll one dread gaze first and if the defender won he can use his dread gaze. Since I play with the advanced conflict rules, who goes first is not a problem for my group. If you play with the normal conflict rules, on p. 125 exists a sidebar (&quot;who goes first&quot;) that gives a good template to follow. So in the case of dread gaze you can either a) compare dex+wits or b) who has the higher &quot;skill&quot; ( in this case I would use the discipline rank).<br /> One Situation where I would make a gaze vs gaze test would be a &quot;stare off&quot;. Lets say Brujah A and Brujah B want to play Presence chicken. They both use gaze and see who runs first. Since they can activate at exactly the same time ( in theory) this is a question of &quot;who is scarier&quot; more than &quot;who goes first&quot;.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps a little ^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T21:20:07-07:00","id":1456278,"title":"","content":"I would have both Dread Gazes work at the same time, meaning both would run away from each other or collapse in terror, depending on successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}